            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Teaching Career</strong><br>\nGlashow has been a prominent educator and researcher. After spending a significant part of his career at Harvard, he joined the faculty of Boston University. Throughout his teaching career, he has inspired many students to pursue careers in physics and has been a mentor to upcoming scientists.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Influence on Particle Physics</strong><br>\nHis work extended beyond electroweak unification. Sheldon Glashow has proposed several theories and models in particle physics, influencing the way physicists understand the fundamental structure of matter. His contributions have had a lasting impact on the study of particle physics and cosmology.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Other Notable Works</strong><br>\nApart from his Nobel-winning work, Glashow has contributed to the development of the quark model, which describes the behavior of subatomic particles. He also predicted the charm quark with James Bjorken, which was later discovered in experiments in 1974, verifying the accuracy of the Standard Model.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
