          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Advocacy for Science</strong><br>\nSheldon Glashow is also known for his advocacy for science education and policy. He has written extensively on the importance of scientific literacy and the role of science in society. His voice has been influential in debates on science education and the funding of scientific research.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal Philosophy</strong><br>\nGlashow's personal philosophy on science emphasizes the beauty and simplicity of physical laws. He believes that understanding the universe's workings is not only a scientific pursuit but also an aesthetic one. His approach to physics is often characterized by seeking elegance in theoretical formulations.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Influence</strong><br>\nThe legacy of Sheldon Glashow's work is evident in the continued relevance of the Standard Model as the predominant theory in particle physics. His contributions to theoretical physics continue to guide experimental research in high-energy physics, and his theories are still a topic of discussion and development in the scientific community.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
